# The build context is the repository root, because the API image carries the
# agents package as well and a context inside api/ cannot see it. That makes
# this file load-bearing: without it every build uploads the whole repository,
# including a virtualenv, node_modules and any encoded footage lying about.

.git
.github

# Virtualenvs. Platform-specific binaries that would be copied in and then
# shadowed by the ones pip installs — slow, large, and confusing when they
# disagree.
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# The web service builds from its own context and needs none of this here.
web/
node_modules/

# Encoded output and source footage. Regenerated by tools/, and the source is
# licensed for analysis rather than redistribution.
dataset-build/
demo-build/
eval/fixtures/

# Infrastructure state, which is not application code and can carry secrets.
infra/
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.backup
**/.terraform

docs/
*.md
!api/README.md

# Local configuration. Nothing in an image should come from a developer's
# machine, and a stray .env baked into a layer is a credential in a registry.
**/.env
**/.env.*
